An optimisation proposal, argued well: the client already computes its predicted position every tick. Sending `Move` means the server recomputes the identical thing, and any disagreement between the two costs a rollback. So send the answer instead:

    public struct PlayerMoveInput : IInputComponentData {
        public float3 Position;   // was: float2 Move
    }

The server writes the received position onto the capsule. Rollbacks drop to zero. Latency feel is unchanged. Bandwidth is comparable. Every test passes, including the two-player one.
